# Check small multiples of known families: in particular the family n = 2 * 5^k we expect; our candidate generation should include p=5.
# As a safety, also brute-force check all n of form 2 * q where q is a prime power <= LIMIT (q odd) that we might have missed.
# But iterating all primes up to sqrt(LIMIT) is expensive; instead check numbers of the form 2 * p^k for primes p in [3..LIMIT//2] where p found by checking 3^{2*p^k} mod p^k etc.
# To be safe but fast, we'll also brute-force test all n <= 2000000 (2e6) directly; that's quick.

